# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CareCircle environment variables. Copy to `.env` (or `.env.local`) and fill in.
# NEVER commit the real .env — only this example file is tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- Database: Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL ----
# Two-role model (see SETUP.md):
#  - DATABASE_URL           -> the LEAST-PRIVILEGE app role (carecircle_app). The running
#                              app uses this, so Row-Level Security is ENFORCED. Demo needs it.
#  - MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL -> the admin/owner connection. Used by drizzle-kit and the seed
#                              script to create tables/policies/demo data. Bypasses RLS (admin).
# Aurora requires SSL (sslmode=require).
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://carecircle_app:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/carecircle?sslmode=require"
MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://ADMIN:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/carecircle?sslmode=require"

# ---- Auth.js (NextAuth v5) ----
# Generate a secret with:  npx auth secret   (or: openssl rand -base64 32)
AUTH_SECRET="replace-me-with-a-random-secret"

# Optional in dev. In production set to your deployed URL (e.g. https://carecircle.vercel.app)
# AUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# ---- Google OAuth (optional sign-in provider) ----
# Create credentials at https://console.cloud.google.com → APIs & Services → Credentials.
# Authorized redirect URI: http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/google
# When set, the "Continue with Google" button lights up automatically (server-side gate).
AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=""
AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=""

# ---- Apple OAuth (optional — needs a paid Apple Developer account) ----
# AUTH_APPLE_ID = your Services ID (e.g. app.carecircle.web).
# AUTH_APPLE_SECRET = the ES256 client-secret JWT (regenerate every <=6 months).
# Redirect URI: http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/apple
AUTH_APPLE_ID=""
AUTH_APPLE_SECRET=""

# ---- Social button visibility (client-side) ----
# These mirror whether the OAuth creds above are set. They only control whether the button
# RENDERS; the server action is the real guard. Google shows unless set to "false"; Apple is
# hidden unless set to "true".
NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_GOOGLE_ENABLED="true"
NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_APPLE_ENABLED="false"

# ---- Demo / judging mode ----
# "1" enables BOTH judge conveniences (leave unset/empty for a real production deployment):
#  - one-click demo-persona sign-in buttons on /sign-in (the seeded Maria / Paolo / Grace /
#    Antonio / Rosa accounts from `npm run db:seed`);
#  - the homepage "Run demo" button: creates an anonymous, persisted guest account scoped (by
#    Row-Level Security) to ONLY the demo circle and lands the visitor on the live dashboard —
#    no sign-up or onboarding. Server-enforced fail-closed in src/lib/auth/demo.ts; needs
#    MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL (the privileged connection) and the seed to be loaded. Guests are
#    wiped on every `npm run db:seed`.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_MODE="1"

# ---- Platform super-admin ----
# Comma-separated emails allowed into the cross-tenant admin console at /admin. These users see
# data across ALL care circles, so keep the list tight. Email is read from the verified session.
PLATFORM_ADMIN_EMAILS="admin@carecircle.demo"

# ---- Email delivery — password-reset & invite links ----
# Provider for transactional email. One of: ses | smtp | resend | console.
#   ses     — Amazon SES (the architecture's choice). Needs AWS creds below + a VERIFIED
#             EMAIL_FROM identity, and your SES account out of the sandbox to email anyone.
#   smtp    — any SMTP server (e.g. Gmail). Emails ANYONE for free with no domain / no approval.
#             Gmail: enable 2-Step Verification, create an App Password at
#             https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords, then set SMTP_* below.
#   resend  — Resend (https://resend.com, free tier). Needs RESEND_API_KEY.
#   console — log the email to the server console (zero setup; great for local dev).
# Leave EMAIL_PROVIDER unset to auto-pick: SMTP when SMTP_* are set, else SES when AWS creds + a
# non-resend.dev EMAIL_FROM are present, else Resend when RESEND_API_KEY is set, else console.
EMAIL_PROVIDER=""
RESEND_API_KEY=""
# SMTP (used when EMAIL_PROVIDER=smtp). For Gmail: host smtp.gmail.com, port 465, user = your
# Gmail address, pass = the 16-char App Password (no spaces).
SMTP_HOST=""
SMTP_PORT="465"
SMTP_USER=""
SMTP_PASS=""
# The "From" address. SES → a verified identity. SMTP/Gmail → your Gmail address. Resend → a
# verified Resend sender (sandbox: 'onboarding@resend.dev').
EMAIL_FROM="CareCircle <onboarding@resend.dev>"

# ---- AWS (Amazon SES email, SNS escalation alerts, S3 uploads, Bedrock AI) ----
# Credentials, in order of preference:
#  1. PRODUCTION (Vercel) — OIDC federation, NO stored keys: trust the Vercel OIDC issuer in AWS
#     IAM, then set ONLY AWS_ROLE_ARN below. Each invocation exchanges Vercel's OIDC token for
#     short-lived STS credentials (see src/lib/aws/credentials.ts + SETUP.md "Vercel OIDC → AWS").
#  2. LOCAL DEV — a static key pair for your IAM user (least-privilege).
# AWS_REGION="us-east-1"
# AWS_ROLE_ARN="arn:aws:iam::<acct>:role/carecircle-vercel-oidc"
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=""
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=""
# SNS topic for urgent escalation alerts (a logged fall, ER visit). If unset, alerts log to console.
# SNS_ESCALATIONS_TOPIC_ARN="arn:aws:sns:us-east-1:<acct>:carecircle-escalations"
# Private S3 bucket for uploads (recipient photos, documents, timeline images). From
# `terraform output s3_bucket_name`. If unset, photo uploads are skipped (onboarding still works).
# S3_BUCKET="carecircle-uploads-xxxxxxxxxxxx"

# ---- Ask CareCircle — RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation), all on AWS ----
# Pipeline: uploaded documents + timeline + audit entries are chunked, embedded with Amazon Bedrock
# Titan, and stored as vectors IN Aurora (the `rag_chunk` table via the pgvector extension, one row
# per chunk, tenant-scoped + sensitivity-tagged). Ask embeds the question, runs a pgvector cosine
# search that RLS automatically filters to the asker's role/sensitivity, and Claude on Bedrock
# writes the grounded, cited answer. Uses the AWS creds above — no external vector DB or API keys.
#
# Embeddings: Amazon Bedrock Titan Text Embeddings v2 (1024-d). Override only if needed. Must be
# access-enabled in the Bedrock console, and your IAM must allow bedrock:InvokeModel on it.
# BEDROCK_EMBED_MODEL_ID="amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0"
#
# Generation: Claude on Bedrock (Converse API). Set to an inference-profile id ENABLED in your
# account/region (ids are account/region-specific), e.g. "us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-...".
# BEDROCK_MODEL_ID=""
#
# NOTE: the rag_chunk table + pgvector extension are created by `npm run db:migrate`
# (drizzle/0025_*, 0026_*). The migration runs `CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector` as the
# admin/owner connection (MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL).

# ---- Scheduled jobs: nightly Daily Digest + daily care scans ----
# Shared secret protecting BOTH cron endpoints (`/api/cron/digest`, `/api/cron/scans`). Call them
# from a scheduler (Vercel Cron, EventBridge, or any pinger) with `Authorization: Bearer <secret>`.
#  - digest (hourly): generates + emails the digest to opted-in members of every circle whose LOCAL
#    clock has reached its `digestHour` and that hasn't been sent yet today. Needs Bedrock (above)
#    and the cross-tenant connection (MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL); sending uses the email provider above.
#  - scans (every 6h, idempotent): refill sweep (auto-opens a task for low-supply meds),
#    missed-dose reconciliation (writes `missed` administrations for yesterday's unrecorded doses),
#    and the decline scan (urgent alert when a vital is out of its safe range 3 days running).
# If unset, both endpoints reject every request (fail-closed) — set it to enable the jobs.
# CRON_SECRET=""
#
# Schedules live in vercel.json; Vercel automatically sends Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET.
